{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c49b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a11-62cd-7c32-94ca-eb83f5233a55"},"sequence":168,"recorded_at":1780531400000331,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"357c7038-eba4-4a96-b13f-85a78cd24f9a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"357c7038-eba4-4a96-b13f-85a78cd24f9a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"357c7038-eba4-4a96-b13f-85a78cd24f9a"},"call_id":"call_01a07a11cd3f7191aa68326b8619bd04","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260906-v8heil) { full }' --format json 2>&1 | head -200\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task record\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ac\\\":\\\"Production behavior demonstrates: one shared test-support core owns production-file selection, fail-closed parsing, and the both-direction harness, and every existing inventory is expressed through it. terminalbackend refusal arms are resolved by executed witnesses that refuse at the production entry point, not by source text mentioning a detail string. Alias-bypass coverage is preserved for every package that had it, proven by a negative test per bypass shape that fails when the core drops that direction. Arm counts before and after are reported with any change accounted for; a floor regresses no package.\\\",\\\"assignee\\\":\\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\\"blockedBy\\\":[\\\"TASK-260906-vmzk0y\\\"],\\\"blocks\\\":[\\\"TASK-260906-2okwyf\\\"],\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"One shared test-support core owns production-file selection, fail-closed parsing, and the both-direction check harness; every existing inventory is expressed through it\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"terminalbackend refusal arms are resolved by executed witnesses that refuse at the production entry point, not by source text mentioning a detail string\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Alias-bypass coverage is preserved for every package that had it, proven by a negative test per bypass shape that fails when the core drops that direction\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The core fails closed on an unregistered site, an orphan row and a site it cannot classify, each control-planted including an import alias and a var binding\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Arm counts before and after are reported per package with any change accounted for; no package regresses its floor\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"The digit-guard census stated bound is completed or widened: code-point, named-rune and strconv spellings are enumerated or explicitly named as outside the classifier\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Mutation battery reports killed over applied on a production-derived denominator with narrowing, arm-deletion and census-only separate, and NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Per-arm behavioural-versus-census kill split is reported, with the behavioural mask verified non-empty\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Candidate tree OID in the outcome document equals the one the Change Request record carries, verified by listing the tree\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\\"done\\\":true}],\\\"children\\\":[],\\\"created\\\":\\\"2026-09-06T07:19:18Z\\\",\\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\":[],\\\"derivedBlocks\\\":[],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Close advisory A6. Twenty hand-rolled go/parser walkers now exist across ten packages, seven added by the two landed Stories, in three architectures for the same idea: terminalbackend resolves a declared row textually (a row passes if the named test source mentions the detail, so a dead arm can resolve through a sibling and the file says so); provhost executes every witness through the production entry point and requires the refusal to come from that arm; provider swaps constructor vars in TestMain and audits the exercised file:line set against AST-derived sites. The weaker bound is the real bound. Extract a shared test-support core carrying the production-file glob, fail-closed parse, and a both-direction check harness, and port terminalbackend from textual resolution to executed witnesses. Each existing walker closes a different blind spot (terminalbackend refuses constructor aliasing outright, provider catches aliases at runtime, provhost keys on identifier names and relies on a separate call-site audit); the shared core must keep the union of those, not the intersection.\\\",\\\"estimate\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"estimated\\\",\\\"scale\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fibonacci\\\",\\\"number\\\":13}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"TASK-260906-v8heil\\\",\\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\":true,\\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\":false,\\\"isBlocked\\\":false,\\\"name\\\":\\\"unify-inventory-machinery-on-executed-witnesses\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/xhigh pair_source=explicit match=not_recommended snapshot=sha256:08c5d671a0c9e2350b1b8c97c08841f378392d0f4ac8edf05ecf155d29ae97bb rationale=\\\\\\\"implementation class rank 1; third convergence leaf, the shared inventory core leaf 2 spent six rounds justifying\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=muse; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260907-39632